<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle market not tested - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle market not tested - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slaughter steers and heifers</p>
<p>were not tested, USDA said. Buyer inquiry modest.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed - None   For the week.</p>
<p>Few bids of $103.00-$104.00 per cwt on a dressed basis reported. Seller interest very limited. Showlists well depleted, given the weekly volume of 100,000 head.</p>
<p>Live basis sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered and FOB, some FOB 4% shrink. Dressed basis delivered (paid on hot carcass weights)</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers -  No reported sales.</p>
<p>Slaughter Heifers - No reported sales</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
